{
  "title": "Granada, Spain",
  "indexDescription": "A couple of days in Granada over Christmas 2009.",
  "description": "We stayed in a house in the Muslim quarter of Granada over Christmas.  The house was in a labyrinth of narrow cobbled streets, stairs and paths on a steep hill.  You find it on the map as the Albaicín, a UNESCO World Heritage site.  It's across a valley from the Alhambra.\n\nWe visited the Alhambra on two days.  I took a lot of pictures of it, but they are not in this collection, which focuses on the rest of the town.\n\nWhen we first arrived in town I parked in a garage.  You drive down a narrow ramp and take a 90 degree turn to enter the underground parking.  Later that day when it was time to leave, we piled into the van and proceeded to the ramp.  I made the 90 degree turn, then the tires started spinning and we wouldn't go any farther.  There was no way to get a running start.  Everyone climbed out except me and I tried a couple more times without luck.  Everyone was watching.  Then I really pressed on the accelerator, spun the tires like crazy and was able to drive out.  Black smoke and the smell of burning tires filled the place.  Later I was lucky to find regular street parking on the hill.\n\nOn Christmas Day we walked down into town and peeked into the cathedral to look at the Christmas services and the architecture.",
  "cNum": 55,
